>The 636 crashes because the interface is in promiscuous mode (it's
>either put in a bridge or you have tcpdump running on it?). This won't
>work with 636. See mailing list archives. 636 has broken monitor mode
>and it crashes often.

>Can you please retry with debug_mask=3D0xffffffff to get full dumps and
>see what kind of frame is being sent? I guess it's an ipv6 neighbour
>solicitation but the request itself might be malformed for some reason
>causing firmware to crash unexpectedly.

>Also, can you try the test without making wlan interface promiscuous
>(on both firmwares, with debug_mask=3D0xffffffff) too, please?

Yes I used promiscuous to set up my station in bridge mode, the firmware cr=
ashed=20
but If don't use promiscuous (put my station in router mode), the firmware =
didn't crash and
I can associate with the access point without problem.=20
You can found in the attached file 4 dmesg file (with/without promicuous) f=
or both version of firmware.
(If I set debug mask=3D0xffffffff there are many lines "htt rx pop" and I c=
an not see all the dmesg, so I=20
only set the mask=3D0xffffff3f).
But I wonder if there will be any progress of the firmware in the future fo=
r promiscuous so that I can=20
set up bridge mode? =20

